# BlueTool's "deepsleep" for the Galaxy S9/Note9: what bluetoothd asks for after a power-off from Settings. Without this
# file BlueTool ran Apple's own sequence, wrote to a device it had not opened ("Error writing bytes ... Device not
# configured"), bluetoothd waited 5 s ("BlueTool timed out running deepsleep script!", "Clean power off failed") and
# aborted (step 91, 16 November). The chip's power is the kernel's (bt=7): opened, and nothing else.
device -D -S
